From: sKyissKy <29267720+sKyissKy@users.noreply.github.com>
Subject: [PATCH] warp: preserve MTK_MEMORY_SHRINK fallback define

Ensure CONFIG_MTK_MEMORY_SHRINK retains its fallback definition when omitted from external CFLAGS.
Signed-off-by: sKyissKy <29267720+sKyissKy@users.noreply.github.com>
---
 Makefile | 2 --
 1 file changed, 2 deletions(-)

diff --git a/Makefile b/Makefile
index 897460e..b3be8d8 100644
--- a/Makefile
+++ b/Makefile
@@ -4,9 +4,7 @@ ifeq ($(CONFIG_WARP_DBG_SUPPORT), y)
 ccflags-y += -DCONFIG_WARP_DBG_SUPPORT
 endif
 
-ifeq ($(CONFIG_MTK_MEMORY_SHRINK), y)
 ccflags-y += -DMEMORY_SHRINK
-endif
 
 ifeq ($(CONFIG_WARP_MEMORY_LEAK_DBG), y)
 ccflags-y += -DMEM_LEAK_DBG
